<PolicyPage
  title="Delivery and collection"
  intro="How your books reach you, what it costs and how long it takes."
>
  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <p>Nothing is charged on this website. You send us a request, we confirm what is in stock and what the postage comes to, and only then do we send you the total and how to pay. Your books are held for you for 48 hours while you decide.</p>

  <h2>Postage</h2>
  <p>Postage depends on the weight and where it is going, so it is quoted on each order rather than fixed. Typically <span class="blank">[usual range, e.g. £3.50–£6]</span> within the UK.</p>
  <p>We post with <span class="blank">[carriers you use]</span>. Once a parcel is sent we pass on the tracking number if there is one.</p>

  <h2>How long</h2>
  <p>Orders are usually confirmed within <span class="blank">[e.g. 24 hours]</span> and posted within <span class="blank">[e.g. 2 working days]</span> of payment. Delivery then takes <span class="blank">[e.g. 2–3 working days]</span>.</p>

  <h2>Collection</h2>
  <p>You can collect instead of paying postage. We tell you where and when once your order is confirmed, and you can pay in cash when you arrive if you prefer.</p>

  <h2>Outside the UK</h2>
  <p>We do post abroad. <span class="blank">[Say whether duties are the customer's responsibility, and any countries you do not post to.]</span></p>
</PolicyPage>
